r one with  respect each vignette that portrayed the  Great War gave players inside to its  mentality scale and effect on human  lives but battlefields draw has been and  always will be large-scale multiplayer  and battlefield one's operations mode is  a definite highlight with historically  grounded maps buried ground in air  combat and improved progression systems  players have several reasons to come  back instead of defending Earth from an  alien invasion  XCOM to twist the narrative humankind is  fighting for survival after being  occupied by the aliens theme of  desperation is set from the start  XCOM to test players and made them  rethink what it means to play a strategy  game it's a symmetric style of battles  fit the feel of guerrilla warfare you're  forced to think steps ahead become  resourceful and be prepared to retreat  you can't win every fight and players  have to deal with the consequences of  failure you'll lose soldiers lose  territories but how you learn from  failure makes X come to a truly unique  experience it's all wrapped into a  cohesive fun and rewarding package that  is an outstanding addition to one of  PC's most acclaimed franchises overwatch  revolutionize class-based team shooters  each character was crafted with  tremendous thought and detail not only  in their aesthetic but in their in-game  abilities as well the game is designed  to encourage teamwork and thoughtful  team composition and it eases players  into these elements in the most helpful  way possible from on-screen prompts to  easily recognizable character animations  and sound design players always know  what's happening but it's up to players  to think critically and band together to  push for victory it's easy to learn hard  to master  Blizzard also spawned a cultural  phenomenon the animated shorts gave  characters deeper backstory and  overwatch cosplay is taking over  conventions it's another stunning  example of how Blizzard precisely crafts  its games whether you like overwatch or  not there's no denying it caused a  paradigm shift and multiplayer game  [Music]
 

